                <pb facs="0785" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg691"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received November 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 591.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 589, of the 15th instant, relative to the prohibition which was
                    placed on the shipment of 307 bales of tobacco, by Mr. Louis Wertheimer, from
                    Cuba to the United States, and to inform you that the case has been duly
                    presented to the Spanish Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
